      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "We originally believed the 2 issues described here are the same root cause, but there was a misunderstanding. In reality, there are 2 distinct bugs:\n\n- Objects will respawn in the last received location, instead of at their origin point.\n\n- In ClientSim, calling \"Respawn\" can trigger a null reference exception.\n\nFor the former, we have a fix that will ship in the next major release.\n\nFor the latter, this will happen when calling \"Respawn\" on a gameobject that has never been enabled. @{629216d852b0321ee7af0c71|full_name} Is it possible that you are doing just that? I'm not sure this is really so much a bug as much as it is undefined behaviour. An object that was never enabled doesn't have an origin position of first activation.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
